WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.013
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.313 --> 00:00:08.514
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.814 --> 00:00:15.182
Unit thirty-four: Success and Failure. In this unit, you will talk about setbacks, success and emphasis.

4
00:00:16.183 --> 00:00:17.045
setback.

5
00:00:17.745 --> 00:00:20.325
setback means a problem that delays progress.

6
00:00:20.625 --> 00:00:22.892
Losing the contract was a big setback.

7
00:00:23.592 --> 00:00:26.116
Your turn. Say: setback.

8
00:00:28.816 --> 00:00:29.852
setback.

9
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:31.921
perseverance.

10
00:00:32.621 --> 00:00:35.909
perseverance means continuing to try despite difficulties.

11
00:00:36.209 --> 00:00:38.371
Her perseverance finally paid off.

12
00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:42.037
Your turn. Say: perseverance.

13
00:00:44.737 --> 00:00:45.924
perseverance.

14
00:00:46.917 --> 00:00:48.011
failure lesson.

15
00:00:48.711 --> 00:00:51.871
failure lesson means something useful learned from failing.

16
00:00:52.171 --> 00:00:54.345
Every failure lesson made him stronger.

17
00:00:55.045 --> 00:00:57.546
Your turn. Say: failure lesson.

18
00:01:00.246 --> 00:01:01.480
failure lesson.

19
00:01:02.483 --> 00:01:03.717
success story.

20
00:01:04.417 --> 00:01:08.227
success story means a person or project that achieved great results.

21
00:01:08.527 --> 00:01:10.701
The café is a local success story.

22
00:01:11.401 --> 00:01:13.984
Your turn. Say: success story.

23
00:01:16.684 --> 00:01:18.114
success story.

24
00:01:19.117 --> 00:01:20.095
self-belief.

25
00:01:20.795 --> 00:01:23.572
self-belief means confidence in your own abilities.

26
00:01:23.872 --> 00:01:26.197
Self-belief helped her through difficult times.

27
00:01:26.897 --> 00:01:29.119
Your turn. Say: self-belief.

28
00:01:31.819 --> 00:01:33.087
self-belief.

29
00:01:34.083 --> 00:01:34.875
growth.

30
00:01:35.575 --> 00:01:38.341
growth means the process of developing or improving.

31
00:01:38.641 --> 00:01:40.792
I've seen real personal growth this year.

32
00:01:41.492 --> 00:01:43.865
Your turn. Say: growth.

33
00:01:46.565 --> 00:01:47.299
growth.

34
00:01:48.283 --> 00:01:49.296
turning point.

35
00:01:49.996 --> 00:01:52.843
turning point means a moment when things start to change.

36
00:01:53.143 --> 00:01:55.549
Meeting my mentor was a turning point in my life.

37
00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:58.460
Your turn. Say: turning point.

38
00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:02.057
turning point.

39
00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:04.016
recognition.

40
00:02:04.716 --> 00:02:07.877
recognition means praise or an award for your achievements.

41
00:02:08.177 --> 00:02:10.548
She received recognition for her research.

42
00:02:11.248 --> 00:02:13.761
Your turn. Say: recognition.

43
00:02:16.461 --> 00:02:17.532
recognition.

44
00:02:18.517 --> 00:02:20.528
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:20.828 --> 00:02:23.570
You did look disappointed when you lost the competition.

46
00:02:24.883 --> 00:02:27.814
I did feel terrible. It was a big setback.

47
00:02:29.117 --> 00:02:31.186
But it became a turning point, didn't it?

48
00:02:32.483 --> 00:02:36.552
It really did. I do believe failure teaches us more than success.

49
00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:41.896
Your perseverance is impressive. Now you're a real success story!

50
00:02:43.183 --> 00:02:46.439
Thank you. I do appreciate your support, Mr. Daniel.

51
00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:50.644
Grammar focus: Emphatic do / does / did.

52
00:02:50.944 --> 00:02:55.079
Use do, does or did before the main verb to add strong emphasis.

53
00:02:55.379 --> 00:02:58.261
It often shows contrast or strong feelings.

54
00:02:58.561 --> 00:03:02.978
For example: I did study hard, but I still failed. I do appreciate your help.

55
00:03:03.278 --> 00:03:06.485
Stress the auxiliary when you speak: I DID study!

56
00:03:07.483 --> 00:03:09.996
Now read and listen. The Value of Failing.

57
00:03:10.296 --> 00:03:13.341
Many famous success stories include years of failure.

58
00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:18.078
Thomas Edison did fail thousands of times before he succeeded.

59
00:03:19.383 --> 00:03:22.393
What turned his setbacks into success was perseverance.

60
00:03:23.683 --> 00:03:27.784
Psychologists say self-belief grows when we learn from each failure lesson.

61
00:03:29.083 --> 00:03:32.731
Recognition may come late, but growth happens at every step.

62
00:03:34.017 --> 00:03:36.332
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:36.632 --> 00:03:39.178
A problem that delays progress is a blank.

64
00:03:39.478 --> 00:03:42.562
A, setback. B, recognition. C, growth.

65
00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:48.248
The answer is A: setback.

66
00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:51.691
I blank want to come, but I'm too busy.

67
00:03:51.991 --> 00:03:54.786
A, do. B, does. C, did to.

68
00:03:58.783 --> 00:04:00.121
The answer is A: do.

69
00:04:01.617 --> 00:04:03.523
He blank try his best yesterday.

70
00:04:03.823 --> 00:04:06.455
A, do. B, did. C, does.

71
00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.055
The answer is B: did.

72
00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:16.084
A moment when things start to change is a blank.

73
00:04:16.384 --> 00:04:20.420
A, turning point. B, success story. C, self-belief.

74
00:04:24.417 --> 00:04:26.637
The answer is A: turning point.

75
00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:32.216
According to the text, what turned Edison's setbacks into success?

76
00:04:32.516 --> 00:04:35.589
A, luck. B, perseverance. C, money.

77
00:04:39.583 --> 00:04:41.676
The answer is B: perseverance.

78
00:04:43.183 --> 00:04:46.915
Now it's your turn to speak. Tell me about a setback that helped you grow.

79
00:04:52.215 --> 00:04:58.629
I did fail my driving test the first time. It was a turning point: I practised more and passed easily.

80
00:04:58.929 --> 00:05:00.430
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:01.417 --> 00:05:05.091
Great work today! You learned eight new words and emphatic do / does / did.

82
00:05:05.391 --> 00:05:08.682
Today's value is hard work. Work hard and never give up.

83
00:05:08.982 --> 00:05:11.611
See you in Unit thirty-five. Goodbye!

84
00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:14.563
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

